When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x0 5 x 0 3cm piece of hard  white tissue with a small amount adherent fat  All frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm modified radical mastectomy with an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The 2 0cm in average diameter nipple is inverted  Lateral to the areolar is a 3 0cm recently sutured incision  At the base of the recent biopsy cavity is a firm  white to tan  gritty nodule  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8  which is variably REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm from the deep resection margin  The nodule is 3 0cm from the superior inferior margins  Medial to the biopsy site and adjacent to the deep resection margin the parenchyma is white  rubbery  with multiple cystic spaces  ranging in diameter from less than 0 1cm up to 0 3cm  This parenchyma covers and expands approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and terminates 2 0cm from the medial resection margin  The parenchyma between the previous identified nodule and axillary tail is composed entirely of fibroadipose tissue  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX 2 and saved frozen  The attached axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm from which multiple lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely  In the adipose tissue at axillary tail nearest the breast is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm white nodule  SECTION CODE  B E  breast nodule  br report_end  , Present.
