dings are compatible with healing biopsy site with exuberant granulation tissue and no evidence of malignancy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin and labeled  lateral margin left breast  stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a stitch marking the new margin  The new margin is inked black  The surface opposite the new margin is focally hemorrhagic and shows red brown granulation tissue focally  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal indurated fatty tissue  with foci of fat necrosis adjacent to the margin opposite the new margin  Submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  anterior margin left breast  stitch marks new margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a stitch marking the new margin  The margin opposite the new margin shows red brown granulation tissue  with foci of fat necrosis and indurated fatty tissue  The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  left axillary lymph node contents   is a fragment of fibrofatty axillary tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm  which on dissection shows several tan pink and tan gray lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The larger lymph nodes are serially sectioned  Most of the larger lymph nodes are partially replaced by fatty tissue  The axillary fibrofatty tissue also shows a tan red cavity  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The cavity is surrounded by indurated fatty tissue  with foci of fat necrosis and hemorrhage  This may represent the previous biopsy site of a possible sentinel lymph node  All the lymph nodes and possible lymph nodes are entirely sub