 for blood vessel invasion  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THREE LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a  left simple mastectomy specimen  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and has an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 12 5cm tan white ellipse of skin  There is an attached stitch at one edge of the ellipse which is taken as the lateral  axillary  position  There is a central slightly inverted nipple and a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ecchymotic region located 2 0cm inferolateral to the nipple  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink and the posterior margin is marked with black ink  There is fascia and a few attached muscle fragments at the deep margin  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm firm ill defined lesion with irregular borders which is located at approximately the 4 o clock position beneath the areola  The lesion extends to 2 3cm of the deep margin and to 5 5cm of the anterior margin  There are a few hemorrhagic tracts in the lesion consistent with a prior biopsy site  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue with a small amount of intervening soft  white fibrous tissue  No other masses or nodules are grossly identified  No lymph nodes are identified in the region adjacent to the stitch  Representative sections are submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with posterior margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections away from lesion  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary contents  is a 4 5x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregular portion of adipose tissue within which two lymph nodes are identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x 0 9x 0 4cm  Each node has soft tan cut surfaces and is bisected  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest node bisected  