ior   posterior and the specimen is inked as follows  superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  and lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal fibrofatty breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm dense firm gritty area  REMOVED_DATE from the superior margin  1 2cm from the inferior margin  1 5cm from the lateral margin  and 1 1cm from the medial margin  1 2cm from the anterior end margin and 0 9cm from the posterior end margin  The specimen is submitted as follows  Section code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior end margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serial section of the biopsy with a described lesion as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior end margin  en face  Final Diagnosis by David C Wilbur M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Present.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 35 CLINICAL DATA  Poorly differentiated CA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  7 CM  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a 14 x 16 x 7 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and a 15 x 7 0cm skin ellipse with a nipple in the center  A firm mass is palpable directly below the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x 6 x 6cm relatively well circumscribed tan to yellow nodular mass with focal cystic and soft regions  the largest cyst is 3cm in diameter and contains bloody fluid  The nodular mass grossly abuts against the posterior and inferior resection margin  Four representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  the closest margin  deep  is submitted in A  A representative section of a tan white  fibrous area that extends from the tumor to the inferior resection margin is submitted in cassette E  Similar fibrous tissue on the posterior deep resection margin is submitted in cassette F  which also contains another section of the fibrous tissue  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 0cm  submitted in cassettes G through L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  WILLETTE Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Tissue Processed Explanation  Additional tissue has been submitted from the axillary region to retrieve more lymph nodes  if possible  CLINICAL DATA  15 0cm right breast tumor  status post neoadjuvant chemoradiation FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  SCATTERED ATYPICAL CELLS BOTH WITHIN DUCTS AND STROMA  SUSPICIOUS FOR RESIDUAL CARCINOMA 2  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES 4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE 5  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Much of the specimen consists of dense fibrous tissue and chronic inflammatory cells  consistent with chemotherapy effect  The atypical cells are present within this fibrous background  and consist predominantly of single cells  The foci containing the atypical cells are  0 2cm from all tissue margins  These atypical cells are not identified within lymphovascular spaces  Cytokeratin stains performed on several of the tissue blocks fail to highlight definitive carcinoma cells  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Willette  REMOVE_MRN and  right modified radical mastectomy  short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 2cm radical mastectomy specimen with an axillary tail  10 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm   marked with the lateral stitch  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse on the anterior surface with an areola that measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm and is grossly unremarkable with a nipple that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior surface is inked black  Sectioning reveals a stellate fibrous area  10 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm   which is located 16 5cm from the lateral aspect  12 7cm from the medial aspect  1 1cm from the posterior margin  1 1cm from the anterior margin  No lesions are identified in the remaining breast parenchyma  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representatives of mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass  from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of uninvolved parenchyma  medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of uninvolved breast parenchyma  lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node candidates from axillary tail   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of fibrous areas  Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Additional tissue from the axillary tissue has been processed  Six lymph nodes were recovered  all of which are negative for carcinoma  Therefore  in total  8 of 8 lymph nodes are negative for carcinoma  Addendum  1 by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Absent.
