tinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 3 specimens  Labeled  left breast lump  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of breast tissue with 2 stitches and a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked entirely in black  the superior half is overlaid with blue  sectioned to reveal an ill defined  firm  tan white nodule  3 0cm in longest dimension  extending to the superior  posterior and lateral resection margins  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A through H   A and H are themost medial and lateral sections respectively  C and D one mass in realtionship to the posterior margin  E and F tumor in relationship to the superior margin   Labeled  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibroadipose tissue  Numerous lymph nodes are dissected  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in largest diameter  The largest lymph node has a tan white yellow  homogeneous and fleshy cut surface  Representative sections of the largest lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes I and J  Representative sections of the remaining lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes K through O  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassette P  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REP