aining for e cadherin  Immunoperoxidase stains for GCDFP show strong staining of the invasive ductal carcinoma cells with weak  patchy staining of the invasive lobular carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  NUMEROUS SCATTERED FOCI  SEVERAL OF WHICH ARE PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  THE LARGEST FOCUS SPANS APPROXIMATELY 0 15CM  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SMALL SCATTERED FOCI  THE LARGEST SPANNING ABOUT 0 15CM   WHICH IS  0 1CM TO THE MARGIN FOCALLY  SEE NOTE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   NOTE  Lymphovascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT  DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  MILD FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  NO CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  A cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stain does not disclose any tumor cells within the specimen  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN ONE LYMPH NODE  SPANNING 0 3CM  SEE TABLE  2  NOTE  No extracapsular extension is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OUT OF TWENTY LYMPH NODES  THE LARGEST SPAN OF THE TUMOR CELLS MEASURING 0 35CM  SEE TABLE  2  NOTE  No extracapsular extension is identified  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  One sentinel and One non sentinel  TOTAL NUMBER OF