e predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new deep margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with a suture on one aspect  The sutured margin is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  The suture designated the true margin on the new deep margin  Sectioning reveals unremarkable parenchyma  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new superior margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of white yellow fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the new true margin on the superior aspect  The sutured margin is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  Sectioning reveals white fibrous parenchyma with no discrete lesions  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette C D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  new medial margin  suture on true margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white yellow portion of breast tissue  with a suture on one aspect designating the true margin of the new medial margin  The sutured aspect is inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  Sectioning reveals no discrete lesions and the specimen is entirely submitted in cassette E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s nam