Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 18 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA 90   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   1 2 CM   FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10   FOCALLY AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  3 FIBOCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  About one half of the tumor mass is mucin secreting  there are microcalcifications present  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  tan yellow  firm to rubbery piece of tissue  with needle localization  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  well demarcated  firm  white  round nodule with a central 0 6cm round  ill defined area of red gray cystic and hemorrhagic spaces measuring between 0 1cm to 0 2cm in diameter  The specimen is submitted in A through E  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH A MUCINOUS COMPONENT  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , Present.
